	<aep:FairValueAssetsAndLiabilitiesMeasuredOnRecurringBasisPolicyTextBlock contextRef="ib1c626024c134ae6ace54353c2c1c081_D20210101-20211231" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmE4Njg2ZGYyZTUxMjRiMzY5ZWM4YjBlMmY4YTA3NWZkL3NlYzphODY4NmRmMmU1MTI0YjM2OWVjOGIwZTJmOGEwNzVmZF81MTQvZnJhZzoxMTQ2OTMwMTdkMjU0YjYyOTBkNDE3YWFlMjM5Y2ExOS90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjExNDY5MzAxN2QyNTRiNjI5MGQ0MTdhYWUyMzljYTE5XzcxODc_0a53dd71-d53b-4dcc-8fca-db8f51a212cb">As required by the accounting guidance for “Fair Value Measurements and Disclosures,” financial assets and liabilities are classified in their entirety based on the lowest level of input that is significant to the fair value measurement.  Management’s assessment of the significance of a particular input to the fair value measurement requires judgment and may affect the valuation of fair value assets and liabilities and their placement within the fair value hierarchy levels.  There have not been any significant changes in management’s valuation techniques.</aep:FairValueAssetsAndLiabilitiesMeasuredOnRecurringBasisPolicyTextBlock>
